{
  "title": "3Sum Closest",
  "description": "Given a list of integers `nums` and an integer `target`, choose three values from three different positions so that their sum is as close to `target` as possible.\n\nReturn that **sum**. Every test has exactly one closest sum.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `3 <= nums.size() <= 200`\n- `-1000 <= nums[i] <= 1000`\n- `-10000 <= target <= 10000`\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "int three_sum_closest(vector<int> nums, int target) {\n    sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());\n    int n = nums.size();\n    int best = nums[0] + nums[1] + nums[2];\n    for (int i = 0; i + 2 < n; ++i) {\n        int left = i + 1, right = n - 1;\n        while (left < right) {\n            int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];\n            if (abs(sum - target) < abs(best - target)) {\n                best = sum;\n            }\n            if (sum < target) {\n                ++left;\n            } else if (sum > target) {\n                --right;\n            } else {\n                return sum;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return best;\n}\n",
  "template": "int three_sum_closest(vector<int> nums, int target) {\n    // Return the sum of three values that is closest to target.\n    return 0;\n}\n",
  "tags": [
    "Arrays",
    "Two Pointers",
    "Sorting"
  ],
